  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1045 AM MST Wed Nov 25 2026\n\nToday and Tonight... \nAn upper level trough moves through the area \ntoday and tonight, the area of low pressure will pass south of the \nregion through Mexico so our CWA will remain dry and have fair \nweather with highs in the low 60s.\n\nThursday through Wednesday... \nFollowing the passage of the trough \nzonal flow will become dominate in the region this will keep us dry \nand have fair weather through Tuesday, with the exception of \nSaturday Afternoon and Monday Evening. On Saturday a shortwave \ntrough will pass over the Rockies into Plains. This shortwave will \namplify a jet streak that will trigger some breezy winds with \ngusts between 20-30 mph in lowlands and up to 40 mph in higher \nelevation areas. Monday evening a shortwave trough will progress \nthrough our area with a weak cold front, this will bring the \npotential for some breezy winds. Gusts between 20-30 mph will be \npossible in the lowlands with gusts up to 40 in higher elevation \nareas during the overnight Monday into Tuesday. Next Wednesday we \nwill see our next real storm system move through the area. Models \ndisagree on timing and pops but there will be a slight chance of \nprecipation throughout the area Wednesday. Windy conditions will \nalso be possible with this storm system.",
